      ],
      "source": "https://www.hursttx.gov/about-us/departments/library/hurst-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Rock Island Station, built in 1903, became the town’s first depot and helped rename the community Hurst in 1909.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hursttx.gov/about-us/departments/library/hurst-history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Arwine Cemetery, with nearly 300 identifiable graves, was declared a historic site in 1977 and remains preserved near Bellaire Shopping Center.",
